  "body": "## What changed\n\nRenames the noun users see for a generated item from **\"Creation\"** to **\"Generation\"**, plus two small UI tweaks on the history page.\n\n- **Rename across UI copy:**\n  - Sidebar: nav item `Creations` → `Generations`, tooltip \"View past creations\" → \"View past generations\", and \"New Creation\" → \"New Generation\" (button + tooltip)\n  - History page heading \"Past Creations\" → \"Past Generations\"\n  - Delete dialog: \"Delete Creation\" / \"delete this creation?\" → Generation\n  - Rename dialog/drawer: \"Rename Creation\" and description copy → Generation\n  - `ChatSection` new-item aria-label, `CreationThumbnail` image alt text\n  - Pricing blurb: \"3D mesh creation\" → \"3D mesh generation\" (now consistent with \"image generation, CAD generation\")\n- **History view toggle:** \"Visual\" button relabeled to **\"Grid\"** (label + `aria-label`).\n- **Sidebar nav button affordance:** the Generations nav item now has a visible surface at rest (`border` + `bg-adam-background-2`) so it reads as a button instead of only lighting up on hover. Hover behavior preserved.\n\n## Why\n\nThe product terminology is standardizing on \"generation\" for a generated model. The sidebar nav item also blended into the background as plain text, so it wasn't obviously clickable.\n\n## Notes for reviewers\n\n- Intentionally **not** renamed: internal identifiers (`CreationThumbnail`, `useCreationThumbnail`, `CreationModeCards`, `CreationType`, etc.), asset filenames (`/creation-mode-*.png|webp` + their `vercel.json` redirects), code/SQL comments, and the \"Creation Mode\" picker concept (which shows no \"Creation\" text to users). These have no user-visible effect; renaming them would be a larger, riskier refactor.\n- `npm run typecheck` passes; pre-commit eslint/prettier ran clean.\n- Unrelated in-progress working-tree changes (DownloadMenu / MeshPreview / OpenSCADViewer / meshConnectivity) were left out of this branch's commit.\n- Button restyle verified via code + typecheck only; the history page is behind Supabase auth, so it wasn't confirmed in a running browser.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
